  "slug": "zero-dna-mirrordna-8a09",
  "summary": "Brieno and MirrorDNA learn discrete tokenizers for nanopore signal and DNA, while benchmark audits in Protify and RPFace stress generalization over leakage-prone evaluation.",
  "synthesis": "The clearest thread is replacing fixed input encodings with learned, modality-aware representations. Brieno applies residual vector quantization to raw nanopore signal and pretrains a Transformer on 118M reads. MirrorDNA learns a tokenizer that enforces reverse-complement symmetry and matches larger models while staying compact. Other items are less about tokenization: MELD, PALM, structRFM, TriTower-m6Am and LESS-PseU build on language-model embeddings or structural information for variant and RNA modification prediction. Protify and RPFace add a methodological counterpoint, reporting task dependence, homology leakage and biased structural benchmarks. The new element is tokenizers that build in biophysical or signal-level structure, alongside stronger scrutiny of how generalization is measured.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
